sections.text:
spokenform.prepare() applies explicit stages in this order:


validate the selected language and protected ranges;


discover literal ranges such as URLs, email addresses, and semantic versions;


obtain or validate optional lexical annotations;


replace protected ranges with internal sentinels and remap annotation offsets;


normalize Unicode independently when enabled;


ask abbr2words for source-aligned structured quantity identities and realize
them with the selected locale’s semantic grammar;


expand lexical abbreviations with exact abbr2words replacements;


verbalize remaining generic numeric forms according to NumberPolicy;


normalize whitespace according to independently configurable controls;


restore protected text and compose stage offset maps.



